1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,420
I'm not in the mood today.

3
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:29,340
Matthew, we'll chat another time.

4
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,780
Chat? Again?

5
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,660
I'm telling you, that Teddy is under some kind of spell!

6
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,580
Victory and defeat are all part of the game.

7
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,900
Mark, I think losing 1 Match might actually be a good thing.

8
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,000
At the very least, it can remind everyone

9
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,340
not to get complacent from now on.

10
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,260
The Autumn Yo-Yo Tournament Team Event

11
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:45,140
is cutting its roster down to 6 people.

12
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,400
What?

13
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,020
Sigh, nice knowing you.

14
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,900
What for? It's not like I'm the
one getting cut from the Team.

15
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,000
Episode 26

16
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,980
Alright, all pass unanimously.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Yay!

18
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,140
They all passed!

19
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:40,380
Of course! You're the only one left.

20
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,780
Chuck, it's all up to you now.

21
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,180
I thought if someone was already out,

22
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,580
Then I wouldn't have to compete anymore.

23
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,980
Yeah, keep dreaming.

24
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:52,380
Chuck, get ready.

25
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,860
Go, Chuck!

26
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:05,820
Don't panic.

27
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,220
Imma go all out!

28
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:10,620
Begin!

29
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,500
Ah! Sleeper!

30
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,340
Return to Sender.

31
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,100
Reluctant to Part.

32
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,020
Satellite Recovery.

33
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:28,860
Scaling the Summit.

34
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,660
Around the World.

35
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:37,980
Shooting Star.

36
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,740
Eiffel Tower.

37
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,020
Front Cyclone.

38
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,300
Baby's Cradle.

39
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,460
Double or Nothing.

40
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,400
Oh no...

41
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:10,620
Coach, isn't there a second chance?

42
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,990
Who said so? Don't try to weasel out.

43
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,860
Chuck, the rules were decided by the whole Team.

44
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:19,260
Looks like you won't be able to compete.

45
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:24,540
No worries, I'll hold down the fort for
the Middle School Division.

46
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,380
That's not the same! What rotten luck.

47
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,220
Coach, someone else still has to drop out. What do we do?

48
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,020
Then we'll proceed to Plan B.

49
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:38,940
Coach, just name a Move.

50
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:45,660
Alright. Use Shooting Star as a Base and create a Variation.

51
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:49,020
Just as I expected.

52
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,420
Piece of cake.

53
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,780
Alright, start!

54
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,660
Shooting Star Variation: Meteor Vortex!

55
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Nice!

56
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:15,420
Shooting Star Variation: Flying Saucer Dragon Ball!

57
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Wow!

58
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:22,620
Leo!

59
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,060
Go.

60
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:31,260
Shooting Star Variation: Meteor Light Wave!

61
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:37,020
Wow, that was amazing!

62
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,460
Matthew!

63
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,340
Go!

64
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:48,540
Shooting Star Variation: Meteor Shockwave!

65
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:52,380
Yeah!

66
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,340
That was awesome!

67
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,300
He nailed it!

68
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,060
Monica!

69
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:07,740
Shooting Star Variation: Lightspeed Saucer!

70
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:14,460
What was that? That doesn't count!

71
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,380
Doesn't count? Monica, get off the stage!

72
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,740
Hmph! I wasn't ready yet!

73
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:23,580
Mini!

74
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,820
Sis, you got this! The slots are already filled.

75
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:36,540
Shooting Star Variation: Phantom Saucer!

76
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,740
Oh no! Sis, what happened?!

77
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:57,660
I haven't even mastered this "Phantom Saucer" move yet!

78
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,060
Sis, don't panic. There's still a chance.

79
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,300
Mickey!

80
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,500
Yeah!

81
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:11,100
Shooting Star Variation: Meteor Ferris Wheel!

82
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:18,300
Coach, what now? Someone's gotta be out.

83
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:23,580
Leo, you're the Captain. What's your opinion?

84
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,980
I think we need another Round.

85
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:27,900
Coach, please pick another Move.

86
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,820
Another round?

87
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,700
If you're willing to drop out, then we don't need to.

88
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,100
What? No way I'm just quitting like that.

89
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:38,460
Fine. I guess this is the only way.

90
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,340
Then I'll name another Move.

91
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,220
Use Front Cyclone as the Base and create a Variation.

92
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,140
Mini, Monica.

93
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,540
This one's a pretty tough move.

94
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,980
You'll both go at the same time.

95
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,900
Be extra careful.

96
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:58,140
Alright, let's start. 1 move decides it all.

97
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:07,260
Front Cyclone Variation: Phantom Cyclone!

98
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:11,100
Front Cyclone Variation: Cyclone Lightspeed!

99
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,500
Mini! Monica! Watch out!

100
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:16,380
If they can do this move 5 times in a row,

101
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:17,700
It's a success.

102
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:19,740
Ready?

103
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,140
Set!

104
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,460
Go, sis!

105
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:29,820
Start!

106
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:38,940
Go, Sis!

107
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:13,980
Yes! That was beautiful, sis! Absolutely beautiful!

108
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:19,260
Looks like it's neck and neck.

109
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:22,110
My Sister clearly won that!

110
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,100
Why?

111
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,020
Because her Finishing Move was way cleaner!

112
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,900
The Competition never said the fastest finish wins.

113
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,820
I think it's at least a tie.

114
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,740
Matthew, could you be any more biased right now?

115
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:33,660
And you, stop siding with Mini so much!

116
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,580
Enough! You two aren't the Judges.

117
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,980
Coach, you make the final call.

118
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,100
Leo!

119
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,940
Hmph, Leo's obviously gonna side with Mini.

120
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,260
Leo, say something.

121
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:25,980
I think Monica wins.

122
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:27,420
Why, Leo?

123
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:29,310
You have to give us a reason.

124
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,740
Yeah! My Sister was clearly faster than Popcorn!

125
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,660
Leo, what's wrong with you?

126
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:36,060
Mickey, calm down.

127
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,750
The reason I said that

128
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,390
is because when Mini was doing the third

129
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,860
Phantom Cyclone,

130
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:42,750
one of her moves wasn't correct,

131
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:44,700
which made the string lose elasticity,

132
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,140
and she briefly lost control of the Yo-Yo.

133
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,030
She recovered it,

134
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,500
but it should still count as a mistake.

135
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,390
Mini?

136
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,860
Mini, you felt it yourself, didn't you?

137
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,500
Yeah...

138
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,700
Sis...

139
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,590
You can't keep letting others win.

140
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,510
Captain, none of us even noticed it!

141
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,980
That shouldn't count as a mistake!

142
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,860
Let's review the recording together, then.

143
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,700
Stop.

144
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:12,540
It was my mistake.

145
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:17,310
See? Mini admits it herself.

146
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,780
Looks like the Captain is being fair after all.

147
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Hold on,

148
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,110
Popcorn's finish was later than my Sister's.

149
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,350
So that doesn't count as a mistake?

150
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,020
Why does my sister have to drop out?

151
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,990
Even though Monica's finish was slower than Mini's,

152
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:30,300
and her moves weren't as clean,

153
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:32,700
she still completed the entire routine flawlessly.

154
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:36,060
Whereas Mini's mistake was a break in her flow,

155
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:37,950
and in a real Competition,

156
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,870
the Judges are all Yo-Yo Experts.

157
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:42,750
They're very strict about fluidity.

158
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,220
A mistake like Mini's

159
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:46,140
would definitely be penalized.

160
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,020
Our Opponents are all top Yo-Yo Players.

161
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,420
And in Team Competition, every single point counts.

162
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,790
So with similar flaws,

163
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,740
I think Mini's was more severe.

164
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,140
That's why I said

165
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,060
Monica wins.

166
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,460
Coach, what do you think?

167
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:12,540
I agree with Leo. Today's Competition

168
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:17,340
has already determined the outcome.

169
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,740
Mini, Chuck,

170
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:22,620
It looks like you two will have to drop out.

171
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,060
Coach!

172
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,460
One more time!

173
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:30,300
Mickey, stop.

174
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:34,140
I... I'll drop out.

175
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:36,540
Sis!

176
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,900
Sis!

177
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,700
Leo!

178
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,180
Sis!

179
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,540
Sis, don't do this.

180
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,900
Let's go fight for one more chance!

181
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:19,260
Mickey, Don't stop me.

182
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,660
Just let me be alone for a bit, okay?

183
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,630
Mini!

184
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,600
I...

185
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,540
It's all your fault! Hmph.

186
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Ah...

187
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,420
We should celebrate, you're buying.

188
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:52,860
I'm paying again?

189
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,780
Shouldn't it be your turn this time?

190
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,180
You passed the Competition!

191
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,100
Treating us is only natural.

192
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,980
Me passing is completely expected.

193
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:06,300
Then let's say it's to celebrate for Popcorn passing.

194
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,770
Alright, I'll treat, I'll treat.

195
00:14:10,780 --> 00:14:12,570
Hey, Mark. Where should we go?

196
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:15,310
You guys go ahead.

197
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:19,260
I have stuff to do. I'm heading out first.

198
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,660
In my heart,

199
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,500
I wanted to help Mini.

200
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,900
But I had to...

201
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:05,820
Why did I have to make this kind of decision?

202
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:00,060
Sis, He's still standing there.

203
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,820
Mickey.

204
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,220
Tell him to go back.

205
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,100
I don't want to see him right now.

206
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,260
Mickey.

207
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,780
Sis told you to go home.

208
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,140
Mickey!

209
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,500
You could totally go to the Coach

210
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,420
and ask them to compete one more time.

211
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,780
Maybe my Sister would have done better than Monica.

212
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:56,220
You never know.

213
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,110
But if we did that,

214
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,060
wouldn't that be totally unfair to Monica?

215
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:01,950
Just think.

216
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,390
It was clearly Mini's mistake.

217
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,860
It was more serious than Monica's.

218
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:06,750
Yet we'd be saying it doesn't count,

219
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,220
and asking for a do-over.

220
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,140
If Monica made a mistake,

221
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,540
she could have asked for a redo too.

222
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:18,300
Besides, based on their regular performance,

223
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:22,140
Monica's skills are actually better than Mini's.

224
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:25,980
Mickey, You know that too.

225
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:29,820
But... my Sister's been preparing for this Tournament

226
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,260
for such a long time.

227
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,180
I know.

228
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:36,540
Personally... I'm with you.

229
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,420
I want Mini to stay and compete.

230
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,300
I want her to stay and train with us.

231
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:47,640
But if we put the Team and the School's honor first,

232
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,020
shouldn't we select the best Players

233
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:51,420
for the Tournament?

234
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,660
Alright, Leo...

235
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,100
I'm heading back.

236
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:06,780
Grandpa!

